 {
  "t": 15409.6,
  "k": "play",
  "text": "A closure is a function that keeps references to variables from the scope it was created in, so those variables stay alive as long as the function does.",
  "dur": 8.981333333333334
 },
 {
  "t": 15409.6,
  "k": "ui",
  "state": "Speaking",
  "note": "",
  "mute": "Mute"
 },
 {
  "t": 15806.1,
  "k": "tts",
  "voice": "bm_fable",
  "text": "That's why closures hold memory: the captured variables aren't freed when the outer function returns, so if you keep a closure around, you keep its captured data around too."
 },
 {
  "t": 15806.1,
  "k": "talk",
  "msgs": [
